From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 7 Sep 2026 13:20:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(initrd): mask NetworkManager-config-initrd.service

The service fails on every boot:

    NetworkManager-config-initrd.service: Main process exited,
        code=exited, status=127/n/a
    Failed to start NetworkManager Configuration (initrd).

127 is command-not-found. Its ExecStart is

    /bin/sh -c "/usr/libexec/nm-initrd-generator -- $(cat /proc/cmdline)"

and no Alpine package ships nm-initrd-generator -- checked every
networkmanager* subpackage in edge. The networkmanager package installs
the unit file; the generator it invokes is never packaged, so the unit
cannot succeed on this distribution at all.

It only surfaced now because a rebuild pulled a newer networkmanager that
started shipping the unit. Nothing here configures networking from the
kernel cmdline, so the service has no work to do even when it is whole.

Masking has to happen in the initrd. `systemctl --failed` reports the
unit as masked, which is misleading: that mask is in the rootfs, while
the unit runs and fails in the initrd before switch-root.

Only this unit is masked. NetworkManager-initrd.service
(/usr/sbin/NetworkManager) and NetworkManager-wait-online-initrd.service
(/usr/bin/nm-online) both call binaries that are present in the initrd
and are left alone.

Verified: full QEMU scenario suite 7/7, 0 failures, 0 coredumps, and no
journal errors in 01_boot_smoke -- which failed on this before.
---
 mkosi.initrd.conf/mkosi.finalize | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/mkosi.initrd.conf/mkosi.finalize b/mkosi.initrd.conf/mkosi.finalize
index eff56d2..3bc4ffa 100644
--- a/mkosi.initrd.conf/mkosi.finalize
+++ b/mkosi.initrd.conf/mkosi.finalize
@@ -6,3 +6,14 @@ set -e
 sed -i "s/^IMAGE_ID=.*/IMAGE_ID=$PMOS_DEVICE/" "$BUILDROOT/usr/lib/os-release"
 # Add VARIANT_ID for UI
 echo "VARIANT_ID=$PMOS_VARIANT" >> "$BUILDROOT/usr/lib/os-release"
+
+## Mask NetworkManager-config-initrd.service.
+# Its ExecStart is /usr/libexec/nm-initrd-generator, and no Alpine package
+# ships that binary -- the unit file is installed, the generator never is,
+# so the service exits 127 on every boot and leaves a failed unit behind.
+# Nothing here configures networking from the kernel cmdline, so the
+# service has no work to do even when it is whole.
+# Only this unit is masked: NetworkManager-initrd.service and
+# NetworkManager-wait-online-initrd.service call binaries that ARE present.
+mkdir -p "$BUILDROOT/etc/systemd/system"
+ln -sf /dev/null "$BUILDROOT/etc/systemd/system/NetworkManager-config-initrd.service"
-- 
2.51.0

